    "profile_text": {
        "body": "AeroVironment describes itself as a leading manufacturer of Unmanned Aircraft Systems, Unmanned Aerial Vehicles, Loitering Munition Systems, and Unmanned Ground Vehicles used for surveillance and reconnaissance by the United States Military, U.S. allies, and commercial industries. The company also says it manufactures High-Altitude Pseudo-Satellites.\n\nIts advanced development group is MacCready Works, which the company says turns concepts into mission-ready autonomous systems. The group is named for Dr. Paul B. MacCready, Jr., and its engineers, roboticists, and AI researchers design next-generation robotic systems across air, land, and sea. The company describes its working approach as the MacCready Method, summarized as build fast, test relentlessly, deploy advantage, with small multidisciplinary teams aiming to move ideas into operational capability in months.\n\nAeroVironment is a for-profit public company headquartered in Arlington, VA, and trades under the ticker AVAV. Its CIK is 0001368622. Its recorded legal exposure is in Virginia, with a count of 152.",
